{"id": "678", "name": "Levocetirizine Dihydrochloride", "slug": "levocetirizine-dihydrochloride-678", "monograph_link": "https://medex.com.bd/attachments/X6nD3znoTgB9YgIDTgAMyzFwxUzwSU/levocetirizine-dihydrochloride-prescribing-information", "drug_class": "Non-sedating antihistamines", "indication": "Urticaria", "indication_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Levocetirizine is indicated in the treatment of symptoms associated with allergic conditions such as perennial allergic rhinitis, seasonal allergic rhinitis and chronic idiopathic urticaria.</div>", "therapeutic_class_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Non-sedating antihistamines</div>", "pharmacology_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">This preparation contains Levocetirizine Dihydrochloride. Levocetirizine is the active (Levo) isomer of cetirizine. It is a new highly effective and well-tolerated nonsedating antihistamine with potent antiallergic properties. It has a two-fold higher affinity for H1 receptors than cetirizine. Levocetirizine has a rapid and long-acting action, allowing once-a-day administration.</div>", "dosage_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\"><strong>Adult and children 12 years of age and older</strong>: The recommended dose is 5 mg once daily.<br><br><strong>Children 6 to 11 years of age</strong>: The recommended dose is 2.5 mg (1/2 tablet or 1 teaspoon oral solution) once daily.<br><br><strong>Children 6 months to 5 years of age</strong>: The recommended dose is 1.25 mg (1/2 teaspoon oral solution) once daily.</div>", "administration_description": "", "interaction_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Levocetirizine is not known to have any interactions with other drugs.</div>", "contraindications_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Hypersensitivity to levocetirizine, cetirizine or its parent compound hydroxyzine. Patients with severe renal impairment (creatinine clearance: &lt;10 ml/min) should not be administered levocetirizine.</div>", "side_effects_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Generally, levocetirizine is well tolerated. However, a few side effects like headache, dry mouth, fatigue and skin rash have been reported rarely.</div>", "pregnancy_and_lactation_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Pregnancy Catagory B. There are no adequate and well-controlled studies in pregnant women. Because animal reproduction studies are not always predictive of human response, levocetirizine should be used during pregnancy only if clearly needed. Since levocetirizine is excreted in breast milk it is not recommended for use by nursing mothers.</div>", "precautions_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Epileptic patients and patients at risk of convulsions. Renal impairment. Pregnancy and lactation.</div>", "pediatric_usage_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\"><strong>Pediatric use</strong>: The recommended dose for the treatment of the uncomplicated skin manifestations of chronic idiopathic urticaria in patients 6 months to 17 years of age is based on extrapolation of efficacy from adults 18 years of age and older.<br><br><strong>Geriatric use</strong>: In clinical studies, each approved indication did not include sufficient numbers of patients aged 65 years and older to determine whether they respond differently than younger patients.<br><br><strong>Hepatic impairment</strong>: No dosage adjustment is required in patients with solely hepatic impairment.<br><br><strong>Renal impairment</strong>:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Mild renal impairment (creatinine clearance: 50-80 ml/min): a dose of 2.5 mg once daily is recommended.</li>\n<li>Moderate renal impairment (creatinine clearance: 30-50 ml/min): a dose of 2.5 mg once every other day is recommended.</li>\n<li>Severe renal impairment (creatinine clearance: 10-30 ml/min): a dose of 2.5 mg twice weekly (administered once every 3-4 days) is recommended.</li>\n<li>End-stage renal disease patients (creatinine clearance: &lt;10 ml/min) and patients undergoing hemodialysis: should not receive Levocetirizine.</li>\n</ul></div>", "overdose_effects_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">No clinically relevant adverse events have been reported in case of overdose. However in the event of overdosage, symptomatic and supportive treatment is recommended.</div>", "duration_of_treatment_description": "", "reconstitution_description": "", "storage_conditions_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Store at a temperature not exceeding 30°C in a dry place. Protect from light.</div>", "brands": [{"id": "12156", "name": "Alcet", "slug": "alcetoral-solution25-mg5-ml", "dosage_form": "Oral Solution", "strength": "2.5 mg/5 ml", "manufacturer": "Healthcare Pharmaceuticals Ltd.", "price": "৳ 50.00", "package_container": "60 ml bottle: ৳ 50.00"}, {"id": "12155", "name": "Alcet", "slug": "alcettablet5-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "5 mg", "manufacturer": "Healthcare Pharmaceuticals Ltd.", "price": "৳ 4.50", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 4.50,(100's pack: ৳ 450.00),"}, {"id": "12154", "name": "Acitrin-L", "slug": "acitrin-loral-solution25-mg5-ml", "dosage_form": "Oral Solution", "strength": "2.5 mg/5 ml", "manufacturer": "ACI Limited", "price": "৳ 55.00", "package_container": "60 ml bottle: ৳ 55.00"}, {"id": "12153", "name": "Acitrin-L", "slug": "acitrin-ltablet5-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "5 mg", "manufacturer": "ACI Limited", "price": "৳ 3.01", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 3.01,(100's pack: ৳ 301.00),"}, {"id": "12157", "name": "Cevozin", "slug": "cevozintablet5-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "5 mg", "manufacturer": "Ad-din Pharmaceuticals Ltd.", "price": "৳ 2.00", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 2.00,(100's pack: ৳ 200.00),"}, {"id": "12158", "name": "Clarigen", "slug": "clarigentablet5-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "5 mg", "manufacturer": "Drug International Ltd.", "price": "৳ 2.00", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 2.00,(100's pack: ৳ 200.00),"}, {"id": "12159", "name": "Curin", "slug": "curintablet5-mg", "dosage_form": "Tab